WEBVTT

00:23.791 --> 00:26.041
Come on.

00:27.081 --> 00:29.631
Come on.

00:32.381 --> 00:34.131
Hey. It's a warship.

00:34.801 --> 00:36.091
Tell Gorm. Hurry.

00:36.761 --> 00:38.761
Wait. Look closely.

00:39.811 --> 00:41.521
They're Askeladd's ships.

00:48.521 --> 00:51.531
We finally made it back to the village.

00:52.031 --> 00:54.741
Well, we survived another year.

00:54.821 --> 00:57.491
And you still haven't died, Bjorn.

00:57.571 --> 01:00.371
We went pretty far.

01:00.451 --> 01:01.291
What?

01:02.201 --> 01:05.371
Hey. It's the sheep. They're still grazing them.

01:06.461 --> 01:09.131
They're trying to fatten them up.

01:09.211 --> 01:12.841
It looks like Gorm's still stingy as usual.

01:21.351 --> 01:22.601
Men.

01:22.681 --> 01:24.641
Thanks for your hard work this year.

01:24.731 --> 01:27.191
Enjoy the winter.

03:07.081 --> 03:08.041
Over there.

03:09.251 --> 03:10.211
NOVEMBER 1012 AD

03:10.291 --> 03:12.831
FEUDAL LORD GORM'S VILLAGE
JUTLAND PENINSULA

03:13.881 --> 03:16.001
There's so much treasure.

03:16.671 --> 03:18.761
They had a huge victory
in the land of the Franks.

03:18.841 --> 03:20.131
BEYOND THE EDGE OF THE SEA

03:20.221 --> 03:21.261
I'm impressed, Askeladd.

03:21.761 --> 03:24.681
-I heard some men died this year.
-Really?

03:24.761 --> 03:27.391
I wonder if they're going to look for new sailors again.

03:28.221 --> 03:30.021
Damn. I can't wait.

03:30.101 --> 03:32.731
If I'm going to sail, I want to sail with Askeladd.

03:32.811 --> 03:35.981
Idiot. You'd die within three days.

03:41.201 --> 03:43.321
Hey. Say you're sorry.

03:56.291 --> 03:57.921
What's wrong with that kid?

04:04.051 --> 04:06.601
Ready? One, two...

04:07.141 --> 04:09.221
Askeladd.

04:09.311 --> 04:11.351
Welcome home.

04:11.891 --> 04:14.231
Hey, girls.

04:14.311 --> 04:15.901
You're so cute.

04:16.561 --> 04:19.651
Hey. I brought you some necklaces.

04:21.651 --> 04:23.151
-I'll take it.
-I want a ring.

04:24.031 --> 04:25.531
Hey, Uncle Gorm.

04:25.611 --> 04:29.541
The girls here aren't modest at all. It's wonderful.

04:30.081 --> 04:32.451
I'm here to talk about a serious matter.

04:32.541 --> 04:33.661
Are you ready to listen?

04:34.291 --> 04:35.121
Listen.

04:35.211 --> 04:37.841
The cost to feed one of your men

04:37.921 --> 04:40.551
is one and one-fourth silver coins per day.

04:41.211 --> 04:43.511
You have 97 men,

04:43.591 --> 04:45.761
so that's 121 coins in total--

04:45.841 --> 04:48.141
You want to talk about money again?

04:48.221 --> 04:50.681
The price of pork increased this year.

04:50.761 --> 04:53.431
If you want to eat pork every day,
then you would need...

04:54.101 --> 04:55.771
Beer is charged separately.

04:55.851 --> 04:58.231
And if you add in the cost of lodging and firewood...

04:58.311 --> 05:00.861
Uncle, stop worrying.

05:00.941 --> 05:02.571
We earned a lot this year.

05:03.031 --> 05:06.451
Give my men plenty of booze and food.

05:06.531 --> 05:08.241
I'll pay.

05:08.321 --> 05:10.991
That's what I was waiting to hear.

05:11.081 --> 05:12.081
I'll buy you a drink.

05:12.621 --> 05:14.081
Bring the celebratory drinks.

05:14.161 --> 05:16.831
We have some good wine, right? Bring it here.

05:18.251 --> 05:20.421
One, two, three...

05:20.501 --> 05:23.011
Uncle. Do you really love money so much?

05:24.051 --> 05:25.921
Is there anyone who doesn't?

05:26.511 --> 05:30.601
Money is great. Just looking at it makes me happy.

05:34.351 --> 05:36.691
Hey, Hordaland. What are you doing?

05:37.351 --> 05:39.231
Hurry up, and bring the wine.

05:41.571 --> 05:42.401
Yes, sir.

05:43.901 --> 05:46.071
Oh, dear. What a troublesome woman.

05:48.661 --> 05:50.281
What a weird name.

05:50.371 --> 05:53.831
That slave girl. Hordaland?

05:53.911 --> 05:56.461
-It's the name of a region in Norway.
-Yeah.

05:56.541 --> 05:58.081
I bought her recently.

05:58.581 --> 06:03.501
She's the daughter of a feudal lord,
but her family lost a battle, and fell to ruin.

06:05.421 --> 06:08.131
She's a beautiful girl, and she was expensive.

06:08.221 --> 06:10.011
But she's slow at work.

06:10.091 --> 06:15.521
Rich girls are useless.
They just have a lot of pride.

06:16.561 --> 06:18.601
-By the way, Uncle...
-What?

06:18.691 --> 06:20.651
Can I ask you to be my witness?

06:21.401 --> 06:24.481
I'm scheduled for a duel before dinner.

06:24.571 --> 06:25.531
A duel?

06:25.611 --> 06:26.861
And...

06:28.491 --> 06:31.491
It's not the slave's fault that she's useless.

06:31.571 --> 06:33.741
You're just bad at using her.

06:33.831 --> 06:34.911
What did you say?

06:37.161 --> 06:38.541
You can make use of anyone...

06:39.541 --> 06:42.381
with the right approach.

06:45.051 --> 06:45.921
What?

06:46.001 --> 06:46.961
What's going on?

06:47.051 --> 06:48.551
It's a duel.

06:48.631 --> 06:50.301
You can do it, kid.

06:50.381 --> 06:52.681
Do it. Don't lose to him.

06:56.561 --> 07:00.601
In the name of Odin,

07:00.691 --> 07:04.021
the duel between Thorfinn
and Askeladd is about to begin.

07:04.691 --> 07:07.401
Each man may choose their own weapon.

07:07.481 --> 07:09.281
If you fight with honor,

07:09.361 --> 07:14.531
your soul shall pass through the gates of Valhalla,
even if you shall die.

07:15.031 --> 07:16.411
Seriously?

07:16.491 --> 07:18.751
He's one of Askeladd's men?

07:19.501 --> 07:22.371
Maybe he'd let even someone
like me sail with him too.

07:23.001 --> 07:26.041
-He's kind of cute, right?
-What?

07:26.131 --> 07:29.011
Askeladd has more money. And he's strong.

07:29.551 --> 07:34.891
The reason for this duel is for Thorfinn
to avenge his father's death.

07:35.971 --> 07:38.641
-Are there any objections?
-No.

07:39.311 --> 07:40.271
No.

07:41.441 --> 07:43.101
Then begin.

07:46.731 --> 07:49.651
Unbelievable. Thorfinn's so stubborn.

07:54.991 --> 07:55.821
Go.

07:55.911 --> 07:57.081
You can do it.

07:57.161 --> 07:58.621
Do it.

07:58.701 --> 07:59.791
You...

08:00.831 --> 08:02.831
got taller.

08:02.921 --> 08:04.331
How old are you now?

08:08.091 --> 08:09.841
You were still only this tall back then--

08:14.131 --> 08:15.011
Thorfinn attacked.

08:16.011 --> 08:17.261
He got up close.

08:19.811 --> 08:22.731
You should go along with making small-talk...

08:23.981 --> 08:25.601
with old men.

08:31.031 --> 08:33.031
-He got up.
-He's okay.

08:34.111 --> 08:36.321
He sent him flying with a single hit.

08:36.411 --> 08:39.031
Idiot. Thorfinn jumped.

08:39.701 --> 08:42.911
He knows that the one with the dagger has the advantage
at close range.

08:44.081 --> 08:45.501
He's stronger now.

08:46.581 --> 08:48.171
-Nice, kid.
-Askeladd.

08:50.131 --> 08:51.511
Do it.

09:03.521 --> 09:04.431
He's good.

09:12.781 --> 09:13.611
Damn.

09:20.201 --> 09:21.541
Nice.

09:22.621 --> 09:23.621
Get him.

09:24.791 --> 09:26.871
Hang in there, kid.

09:30.671 --> 09:31.881
Hey, Thorfinn.

09:33.461 --> 09:37.591
Your father... What was his name?

09:38.761 --> 09:42.641
Tho... Tho... Tho...

09:42.721 --> 09:43.851
It's Thors.

09:45.431 --> 09:48.351
Thors. That's right.

09:48.441 --> 09:51.231
Getting old is making me forgetful.

09:55.531 --> 09:57.401
But you know...

09:57.491 --> 10:03.041
I know you're in the middle of getting revenge,
so I feel bad saying this.

10:03.121 --> 10:05.661
I've killed a lot of people, you know.

10:05.751 --> 10:09.541
I can't quite remember your father.

10:10.671 --> 10:13.251
Did I really kill him?

10:13.341 --> 10:15.301
Did I kill Thoril?

10:16.341 --> 10:20.051
Hey. Do you remember how I killed him?

10:20.141 --> 10:21.301
What if...?

10:21.391 --> 10:23.851
Well, maybe you're wrong.

10:25.431 --> 10:26.731
You bastard.

10:27.931 --> 10:30.191
If you had fought him with honor,

10:31.231 --> 10:33.941
my father would never have lost to you.

10:36.031 --> 10:38.201
During that fight,

10:38.281 --> 10:39.321
you...

10:46.451 --> 10:48.501
You took me hostage.

10:48.581 --> 10:51.331
Oh, that's right. I remember now.

10:51.421 --> 10:55.211
He's that idiot who put down his sword
to save a kid's life.

11:13.111 --> 11:15.771
What did he do just now?

11:21.411 --> 11:23.491
Don't get so worked up.

11:23.571 --> 11:25.781
You haven't trained enough, kid.

11:26.951 --> 11:29.251
Damn you.

11:44.391 --> 11:46.561
Bjorn. Pick him up.

11:46.641 --> 11:47.681
Sure.

11:50.021 --> 11:51.181
I'm hungry.

11:51.851 --> 11:53.101
Oh, that's right.

11:54.151 --> 11:55.021
Uncle.

11:56.901 --> 12:00.111
I want to eat some lamb breast.

12:00.191 --> 12:01.951
Roasted with herbs.

12:25.261 --> 12:26.761
I've been waiting for this.

12:31.181 --> 12:32.981
It's so cold.

12:33.061 --> 12:35.601
Hey. Aren't you supposed to guard the ship?

12:35.691 --> 12:38.651
I got out of it. Thorfinn said he doesn't want to switch.

12:39.151 --> 12:42.531
You mean he's in a bad mood because he lost?

12:42.611 --> 12:45.781
He's always been like that.

12:47.121 --> 12:49.031
He feels comfortable there.

12:49.991 --> 12:52.411
It used to be his father's ship.

12:53.461 --> 12:54.961
Just leave him alone.

13:02.461 --> 13:04.341
Not bad.

13:04.421 --> 13:05.551
Askeladd.

13:06.591 --> 13:10.101
Today's duel was amazing.

13:10.181 --> 13:11.601
What? Really?

13:13.231 --> 13:15.811
You threw him at the end, right?

13:15.891 --> 13:19.271
How did you do that? That was so cool.

13:19.941 --> 13:21.531
But you know, captain...

13:21.611 --> 13:24.321
Are you sure about taking a kid
like him sailing with you?

13:24.401 --> 13:26.911
What if he attacks you while you sleep?

13:26.991 --> 13:29.121
I'll be fine.

13:29.201 --> 13:31.491
He could never do it.

13:35.001 --> 13:36.581
What do you mean?

13:36.671 --> 13:39.631
He's a warrior, too, you know.

13:39.711 --> 13:43.381
He'd only accept victory with honor.

13:48.131 --> 13:52.221
He's held back by his past, and his pride.

13:57.691 --> 13:59.981
It's you again, Horda.

14:00.481 --> 14:03.231
You're in the way. Clean it up. Hurry.

14:03.821 --> 14:06.491
You're not a noblewoman anymore.

14:06.571 --> 14:09.911
Stand up, you clumsy girl.

14:09.991 --> 14:11.991
I don't get it.

14:12.621 --> 14:14.741
If I had to live without pride,

14:14.831 --> 14:17.161
I'd rather kill myself.

14:19.751 --> 14:22.131
What's wrong? Did I say something funny?

14:22.211 --> 14:24.001
No. It's not you.

14:28.011 --> 14:29.721
Look.

14:29.801 --> 14:32.011
It's terrible.

14:32.101 --> 14:35.101
Don't forget, you're just a slave.

14:35.181 --> 14:37.271
The guy who's a slave to money holds a whip,

14:37.351 --> 14:41.311
and pretends to be the master
of the slave he bought with his money.

14:43.901 --> 14:45.981
He just doesn't realize it himself.

14:47.031 --> 14:50.281
Everyone is a slave to something.

15:07.261 --> 15:08.591
You upset?

15:16.561 --> 15:17.721
Father.

15:33.451 --> 15:37.201
Hey. Crybaby.

15:47.051 --> 15:48.881
Does it hurt, kid?

15:50.011 --> 15:51.631
Do you want to get revenge?

15:55.601 --> 15:57.681
Well, you're my son.

15:57.761 --> 16:01.101
If I told you not to seek revenge, you wouldn't listen.

16:01.941 --> 16:03.521
This is a problem.

16:04.771 --> 16:06.361
I don't know what to say.

16:08.071 --> 16:10.991
Maybe you'll just have to realize it on your own.

16:13.781 --> 16:15.701
I told you, right?

16:15.781 --> 16:18.741
You don't have any enemies.

16:18.831 --> 16:21.161
No one has any enemies.

16:29.501 --> 16:32.631
A true warrior doesn't need a sword...

16:51.151 --> 16:54.111
Master Gorm told me

16:54.201 --> 16:56.201
to bring you some food.

17:19.301 --> 17:22.601
Hey. Are you a slave too?

17:22.681 --> 17:23.891
What?

17:23.981 --> 17:26.601
Well, you're eating out here.

17:28.351 --> 17:30.111
I'm a warrior.

17:30.191 --> 17:31.691
Unlike you,

17:31.781 --> 17:33.991
I can eat wherever I like.

17:35.071 --> 17:36.491
Really?

17:36.571 --> 17:41.121
But I feel like you're the same as me.

17:42.581 --> 17:44.371
I have no idea how a slave feels.

17:45.121 --> 17:50.081
If I were you, I'd kill Gorm and run away.
I'd kill everyone who came after me too.

17:51.751 --> 17:54.341
Kill him? I could never kill someone.

17:56.471 --> 17:58.841
Then you'll be a slave for the rest of your life.

17:58.931 --> 18:00.141
It's your choice.

18:06.891 --> 18:08.271
If I run away...

18:08.771 --> 18:10.771
Run away as far as I can...

18:10.861 --> 18:13.731
If I run away to the other side of the ocean,

18:13.821 --> 18:16.281
then what's there?

18:19.911 --> 18:22.411
There's probably nothing there, right?

18:23.451 --> 18:25.791
No matter how far I go, it'd be the same as here.

18:25.871 --> 18:28.671
Just filled with wars, and slave traders.

18:46.181 --> 18:47.231
Far west,

18:48.271 --> 18:49.601
across the sea,

18:50.901 --> 18:52.231
there is a land called

18:53.271 --> 18:54.231
Vinland.

18:55.321 --> 18:57.191
It's warm.

18:57.281 --> 18:58.741
And fertile.

18:58.821 --> 19:00.491
A faraway land,

19:00.571 --> 19:03.911
where neither slave traders
nor the flames of war reach.

19:05.831 --> 19:08.121
No one would be able

19:08.201 --> 19:09.581
to find you there.

19:13.501 --> 19:16.501
Does such a place truly exist?

19:52.121 --> 19:54.751
AUGUST 1013 AD
VICINITY OF JELLING, DENMARK

20:00.011 --> 20:04.931
The finest warriors
from clans all over Denmark are gathering.

20:05.471 --> 20:06.471
In addition,

20:06.551 --> 20:10.681
four of our Jomsvikings brigades are hastening
to join them.

20:11.731 --> 20:14.151
Everything is proceeding as planned

20:14.231 --> 20:16.151
for the upcoming campaign.

20:22.701 --> 20:24.571
The time has finally come.

20:24.661 --> 20:27.411
We must show those insolent English scoundrels

20:27.951 --> 20:30.371
the power of the king.

20:31.411 --> 20:32.251
Sir.

20:32.331 --> 20:33.671
Yes, sir.

20:33.751 --> 20:38.291
We will fight without yield
to achieve Your Highness's goal of capturing England.

20:41.211 --> 20:43.051
Where's Canute?

20:43.131 --> 20:44.801
He's here, right?

20:45.221 --> 20:46.181
Yes.

20:46.261 --> 20:48.891
His Highness has already arrived in Jelling.

20:48.971 --> 20:52.311
He's resting to prepare to march.

20:52.391 --> 20:56.191
Your Highness. Are you sure,
you don't want to change your mind?

20:56.271 --> 20:57.861
Ragnar.

20:57.941 --> 21:01.071
There's no need for His Highness Canute
to come along.

21:02.151 --> 21:04.861
He's a candidate to succeed the throne.

21:04.951 --> 21:07.491
I must give him a chance
to display valor on the battlefield,

21:07.571 --> 21:09.621
so that he doesn't lose to his brother Harald.

21:09.701 --> 21:14.331
But His Highness doesn't
have much experience on the battlefield.

21:14.751 --> 21:16.581
Ragnar.

21:16.671 --> 21:19.091
I'm worried for Canute's safety as well.

21:20.131 --> 21:23.591
However, we're the leaders of the Vikings.

21:23.671 --> 21:26.591
If we don't demonstrate valor,
the people will not follow us.

21:28.011 --> 21:30.181
We shall sail tomorrow morning.

21:53.621 --> 21:56.871
In August of 1013 AD,

21:56.961 --> 22:01.541
a Danish and Viking fleet, led by King Sweyn,

22:01.631 --> 22:05.381
invaded the northern part of England,
starting from the Humber River.

22:06.591 --> 22:08.381
In the region of Gainsborough,

22:08.471 --> 22:11.351
five major cities were taken,

22:11.431 --> 22:16.931
and the main army continued
their advance south over land with great speed.

22:17.981 --> 22:21.811
They overran the region,
as they continued their advance.

22:23.941 --> 22:30.911
However, their steady advance came
to a temporary halt...

22:30.991 --> 22:32.621
LONDON

22:32.701 --> 22:35.581
at the merchant town of London.

22:38.161 --> 22:41.171
OCTOBER 1013 AD
LONDON, ENGLAND

23:02.981 --> 23:06.941
What's wrong? Bring it on.

23:07.031 --> 23:10.151
This is a fun war.
